## RA-6 completion decision

This architecture is decision-complete for direct implementation planning when all statements below
hold:

- the winning graph-queue shape is used without promoting research code;
- the current upstream artifact mismatch is handled by explicit adapters, not assumed away;
- additive Description and Requirements handoff exporters seal current outputs without wiring or changing
  their default flows;
- direct Research and Plan phases are artifact boundaries, not skills;
- the production seat policy is two blind semantic seats per graph node;
- every write is confined to an external authorized run root;
- readiness and owner approval remain separate;
- the existing Atom Building Machinery request schema is the downstream byte contract; and
- all sixteen cases above are required before the machinery may be called complete.

